enum CircuitIsolation {
    FULL
    LESS_THAN_1
    LESS_THAN_2
    LESS_THAN_3
    NONE
}

note left of CircuitIsolation
    An Enum that represents how isolated each EVC should be from each other.

    FULL represents that any two EVCs should not be part of the same AssetGroup.
    LESS_THAN_1 represents that they should not be part of more than 1 AssetGroup.
    LESS_THAN_2 represents the same but with no more than 2 AssetGroups.
    LESS_THAN_3 represents the same but with no more than 3 AssetGroups.
    NONE represents that any two EVCs can share as many AssetGroups as needed.
        - Prioritizes uptime than constraint guarantees.
end note

enum IsolationEnforcement {
    COMPLETE
    UNLESS_NECESSARY
    NONE
}

note left of IsolationEnforcement
    An Enum that represents how much we want to enforce the isolation constraint.

    COMPLETE represents that any two EVCs must ALWAYS enforce their isolation constraint. Drop if it cannot.
    UNLESS_NECESSARY represents that enforcement should be maintained unless it is impossible to guarantee.
    NONE represents that enforcement is lax.
        - Prioritizes uptime than constraint guarantees.
end note

